1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,676
Every decade brings faster software and

2
00:00:02,676 --> 00:00:04,940
smarter AI tools promised to hand

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,312
back our afternoons,

4
00:00:06,312 --> 00:00:08,714
yet knowledge workers end up busier

5
00:00:08,714 --> 00:00:09,400
than ever.

6
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,653
In his 1865 book The Coal Question,

7
00:00:11,653 --> 00:00:14,551
economist William Stanley Jevons spotted why:

8
00:00:14,551 --> 00:00:17,126
when James Watt's efficient steam engine

9
00:00:17,126 --> 00:00:18,736
burned less coal per job,

10
00:00:18,736 --> 00:00:21,762
Britain's total coal consumption surged instead

11
00:00:21,762 --> 00:00:22,470
of falling.

12
00:00:22,470 --> 00:00:25,247
Making an input cheaper multiplies demand.

13
00:00:25,247 --> 00:00:27,297
When email and AI make drafting

14
00:00:27,297 --> 00:00:29,016
messages ten times faster,

15
00:00:29,016 --> 00:00:32,454
workplaces quietly generate ten times more messages,

16
00:00:32,454 --> 00:00:32,850
decks,

17
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:33,710
and meetings.

18
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:36,816
Beat Jevons Paradox by capping output volume:

19
00:00:36,816 --> 00:00:39,301
when automation saves you five hours

20
00:00:39,301 --> 00:00:39,784
a week,

21
00:00:39,784 --> 00:00:42,268
immediately wall those hours off for

22
00:00:42,268 --> 00:00:44,270
flagship assets or real rest.

23
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:46,722
Never let efficiency gains leak back

24
00:00:46,722 --> 00:00:47,948
into inbox volume;

25
00:00:47,948 --> 00:00:50,400
bank saved hours into calm leverage.
